WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
Nearly one in six children taking glp-1 drugs show nutritional deficiencies in a new study. This

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:13.120
is Peptides Weekly, episode two, education and evidence, never-dosing advice. An observational

00:00:13.120 --> 00:00:19.280
analysis of insurance claims data linked glp-1 receptor agonists to documented nutritional

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:25.280
deficiencies in nearly one in six children. The study examined real-world prescribing records

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:30.680
rather than a controlled trial. Researchers tracked field prescriptions and subsequent laboratory

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:36.680
results for vitamin and mineral shortfalls. No causal mechanism was established in the data set.

00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:42.840
The analysis covered multiple GLP-1 agents used for type-2 diabetes or weight management.

00:00:43.440 --> 00:00:48.800
Claims databases capture routine care but miss unrequited supplements or dietary changes.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:54.820
A Yale review of online platforms found multiple sites supplying GLP-1 medicines

00:00:54.820 --> 00:01:00.420
after only a questionnaire and without an in-person or video visit by a licensed clinician.

00:01:00.760 --> 00:01:05.880
The study documented the absence of required medical evaluation in the sales process.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:11.880
Researchers classified the model as direct-to-consumer access that bypasses standard oversight.

00:01:12.660 --> 00:01:19.300
Platforms required self-reported height, weight, and medical history but did not verify details with a prescriber.

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.820
The review covered several high traffic sites operating in the United States.

00:01:23.820 --> 00:01:29.460
reports. No regulatory action was described in the report. Swedish Pharmacovigilans records

00:01:29.460 --> 00:01:35.120
show an increase in adverse reaction reports tied to semi-glutide in the most recent reporting

00:01:35.120 --> 00:01:41.160
period. The data come from the National Spontaneous Reporting System and do not include confirmed

00:01:41.160 --> 00:01:47.180
causality assessments. Reports included gastrointestinal events and other side effects already known

00:01:47.180 --> 00:01:52.780
from clinical trials. The National Agency collects voluntary submissions from health care professionals

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:58.900
and patients. An investigative feature examined unregulated peptide products sold for recovery

00:01:58.900 --> 00:02:04.520
and performance. The reporting contrasted marketing claims with documented cases of contamination

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:10.480
and adverse effects in users. No controlled human trials supported the promoted benefits for

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:16.300
the products discussed. The article described products labeled for research use only that reached

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:22.400
consumers through online vendors. Laboratory testing cited in the piece revealed inconsistent purity

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:27.740
across batches. Cyclists and other athletes were among the users interviewed for the story.

00:02:28.320 --> 00:02:36.180
A laboratory study in cell and animal models identified IGF-2BP3 as a regulator that stabilizes

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:44.300
NPY-1R messenger RNA and shifts macrophages toward an M1 phenotype linked to aneurysm rupture.

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:50.680
The work used molecular assays and rodent aneurysm models. Human data were not reported.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:03:00.220
Researcher's measured changes in M6A modification on the NPY-1R transcript after IGF-2BP-3 knockdown.

00:03:00.900 --> 00:03:05.560
Macrophage polarization was assessed by surface markers and cytokine profiles.

00:03:06.180 --> 00:03:11.080
The pathway was tested in both in vitro cultures and in vivo aneurysm induction.

00:03:11.880 --> 00:03:17.200
This week's spotlight looks at semi-glutide and the broader GLP-1 receptor agonist class.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:22.320
Cemaglutide is a long-acting analogue of the gut hormone GLP1.

00:03:22.940 --> 00:03:28.900
It binds the GLP1 receptor on pancreatic beta cells to increase glucose-dependent insulin

00:03:28.900 --> 00:03:31.880
release and on alpha cells to suppress glucagon.

00:03:32.460 --> 00:03:37.460
The same receptor activation in the brain reduces appetite and slows gastric emptying.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:45.620
In the sustained 6-trial, 3,297 adults with type 2 diabetes at high cardiovascular risk

00:03:45.620 --> 00:03:51.160
received once-weekly subcutaneous semaglutide or placebo for 104 weeks.

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:55.680
That result confirmed non-inferiority and suggested superiority.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:03.140
In the select trial, 17,604 adults with overweight or obesity but without diabetes

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:10.180
received 2.4 mg weekly semaglutide or placebo for a mean 39.8 months.

00:04:10.180 --> 00:04:16.360
The same composite endpoint occurred in 6.5% versus 8.0%.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:20.000
That established a cardiovascular benefit in this population.

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:26.960
The Pioneer program tested oral semi-glutide in more than 8,000 adults across eight phase

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.760
three trials lasting up to 78 weeks.

00:04:30.480 --> 00:04:38.260
Doses of 7 mg and 14 mg once daily lowered HBA1C and body weight more than placebo.

00:04:38.260 --> 00:04:43.320
Citigliptin, Ampagliflosen, Lyraglutide, and Dulaglutide.

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:48.420
Gastrointestinal events were the most frequent side effects and were usually transient.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:55.000
A post-hoc analysis of a 32-week randomized trial found that Semaglutide increased the

00:04:55.000 --> 00:05:00.100
reactive hyperimic index from baseline, but the change did not reach significance versus

00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:00.640
placebo.

00:05:01.640 --> 00:05:07.260
E-selectin fell significantly versus placebo, while other cell adhesion markers showed mixed

00:05:07.260 --> 00:05:14.260
responses. Cost effectiveness modeling using Sermount 5 head-to-head data estimated that maximum

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:20.480
tolerated tears epitide produced lower total costs and higher quality adjusted lyphiers than

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:25.620
maximum tolerated semi-glutide in adults with obesity or overweight without diabetes.

00:05:26.480 --> 00:05:31.720
Worth knowing that an observational analysis of insurance claims shows nutritional deficiencies

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:36.640
appear in nearly one in six children prescribed GLP1 receptor agonists.

00:05:37.240 --> 00:05:40.800
That indicates a need for laboratory monitoring in this age group.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:46.520
Spontaneous reporting data from Sweden record a recent increase in adverse event filings

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:47.480
for semi-glutide.

00:05:48.080 --> 00:05:53.320
That underscores the value of ongoing pharmacovigilance for approved GLP1 medicines.

00:05:54.180 --> 00:06:01.480
Laboratory work on IGF2BP3 and aneurysm rupture illustrates how basic peptide signaling research

00:06:01.480 --> 00:06:06.800
can identify new molecular targets. Those findings remain at the cell and animal stage.

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:11.580
That's peptides weekly. This show is education, not medical advice.

00:06:12.180 --> 00:06:15.160
Talk to your own clinician before acting on anything you heard.

00:06:15.780 --> 00:06:18.160
I'm Patrick in Vancouver. See you next week.

